Modifications made for Perceval
-------------------------------
The following components are new or substantially modified relative to the
upstream verl release:

  * verl/utils/reward_score/hallu_token_reward*.py
        Perception-centric reward functions that combine an LLM-as-judge
        outcome verifier with a PRM-based process verifier and a token-position
        finder that maps PRM-flagged sub-sentences to response token spans.

  * verl/workers/reward_manager/trm.py
        Threaded reward manager with retry / fail-task-logging support.

  * verl/workers/reward_manager/naive_record.py
        Record-keeping variant of the naive reward manager.

  * verl/trainer/ppo/core_algos.py
        New advantage estimator `trm` implementing Eq. 3 of the paper:
            Â'_{i,t} = Â_i − α · m_{i,t} · |Â_i|
        where α (= `penalty_percentage`, default 0.1) is the penalty
        strength and m_{i,t} is a token-level mask derived from the
        sub-sentence spans returned by PERCEVAL. Selected via
        `algorithm.adv_estimator=trm` with optional overrides on
        `algorithm.penalty_percentage`.

  * perceval/prompts/prompt_design.py
        Verifier prompt templates used by the reward functions.

  * examples/perceval/
        End-to-end training and serving scripts driven by env vars instead of
        hard-coded paths.
